      "content": "i see. so when you mention things like 'dependency patterns' or the idea that communal living might reduce 'individual responsibility,' are you saying that these specific cultural/religious markers are inherently indicators of lower social or economic stability? basically, are we saying that these traditional or minority-centric lifestyles are fundamentally less reliable from a risk assessment perspective than a standard western, individualistic model?",
